 "path": "memory/continual_arc_marker_template.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC: recolor placements of marker-defined template\n\nObserved solved task (task-6caa3ae2): The input is a noisy binary grid (background colors 0/1) with a small shape drawn in a third color (demo used 5; test used 7). Treat all marked-color cells as a template, preserving their relative coordinates. Search translations of the template where every corresponding cell in the binary background is 0; recolor those cells with the marker color. Keep the original template and all other cells unchanged. The output can contain several matching placements. A simple brute-force scan over every possible top-left translation works: for each marked offset, require the candidate cell to be zero; recolor all offsets for every valid match. The marker shape need not be contiguous. In the solved test, the six-cell 7 template matched several translated zero-pattern locations; only those matches were recolored."
}
